From 342ead2ca4e216e9ae3b143e3f0101e83214f21f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Destrudos6 <3411622425@qq.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:36:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] Make translation concurrency and batch size
 user-configurable

Some providers reject high concurrency, and single huge requests suit
others better, so both knobs now live in the bisub settings screen:

- Parallel requests (1-32, default 12): the batch pool is created per
  translation with the configured size instead of a fixed 12-thread
  static pool; shutdown only stops new submissions, in-flight batches
  keep running
- Lines per request (1-2000, default 40): 2000 equals the unique-line
  cap, i.e. the whole video goes out in one request. Invalid or missing
  values fall back to the defaults, values are clamped on load

The read timeout of each request now grows with its batch size
(max(60s, 2s per line)) because non-streaming chat completion
endpoints only start replying once the whole answer is generated, and
a whole-video request can legitimately take many minutes before the
first byte arrives. The shared OkHttp connection pool is reused via
newBuilder().
